# Stock Expectation — Scheduled Tasks
# All times are interpreted as KST (Asia/Seoul) because of the explicit
# TZ= line below. Earlier revisions of this file used "UTC times with
# KST comments" but the cron daemon on this host runs under the system
# timezone (KST), which made every line silently fire at the wrong wall
# clock — the 2026-05-18 21:00 KST US briefing miss was diagnosed back
# to this. With `TZ=Asia/Seoul` here, the `H M * * D` fields below mean
# exactly what they read.
#
# Install:
#   crontab scheduler/crontab.example
#
# Scheduled LLM jobs use `codex exec` with gpt-5.6-sol/high by default. No API
# key is needed; authentication comes from the host's Codex CLI session.
#
# Environment variables:
#   TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN — for Telegram delivery
#   TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID — target Telegram chat
#   FMP_API_KEY — (optional) for enhanced US data
#   CODEX_MODEL — (optional) model override for account availability
#
# Logs written to ~/logs/stock-expectation/

SHELL=/bin/bash
# nvm-managed node is required by the `codex` CLI subprocess.
# Without the nvm bin dir on PATH, cron-triggered codex-cli runs fail with
# `/usr/bin/env: 'node': No such file or directory` (exit 127) — observed
# on the 2026-05-19 00:00 KST US mid-session briefing. Update this path
# when nvm gets a different version pinned as default.
PATH=/home/cwh/.local/share/nvm/v22.20.0/bin:/home/cwh/.local/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# CRON_TZ pins the schedule-parsing timezone (vixie cron / cronie); without
# it the daemon reads schedule fields in the daemon's host timezone, which
# may not be KST on every box. TZ separately sets the child process env so
# the briefing scripts see the right wall clock for logging/datetime.
CRON_TZ=Asia/Seoul
TZ=Asia/Seoul
PROJECT=/home/cwh/projects/stock-expectation
LOG_DIR=/home/cwh/logs/stock-expectation

# === Codex CLI jobs ===
# Uses `codex exec` with bin/stock-cli and the host's Codex authentication.

# Korean market briefing — 07:00 KST Mon-Fri (before KR market opens 09:00)
0 7 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/daily_briefing.py --market KR --mode codex-cli >> $LOG_DIR/briefing_kr.log 2>&1

# US market pre-market briefing — 21:00 KST Mon-Fri (US pre-market starts ~22:00 KST)
0 21 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/daily_briefing.py --market US --mode codex-cli >> $LOG_DIR/briefing_us.log 2>&1

# US market mid-session briefing — 00:00 KST Tue-Sat
# US regular trading runs 22:30-05:00 KST during EDT (Mar-Nov) and shifts
# one hour later during EST (Nov-Mar) — KR-to-ET offset is 13h in EDT and
# 14h in EST. So 00:00 KST = 11:00 ET (EDT, ~1.5h into session) or
# 10:00 ET (EST, ~30 min after open). Both are firmly inside US regular
# trading and produce a useful mid-session read either way.
# Day-of-week filter is Tue-Sat (2-6) so we get exactly the five US
# trading days: Mon trading -> Tue 00:00 KST, ..., Fri trading -> Sat
# 00:00 KST. Sun and Mon 00:00 KST are skipped (US market closed).
0 0 * * 2-6 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/daily_briefing.py --market US --mode codex-cli >> $LOG_DIR/briefing_us.log 2>&1

# Monthly ISA contribution briefing — 07:37 KST on the 1st (off the :00 mark).
# Adjust the day-of-month and --amount to your contribution schedule; the
# amount is ALWAYS explicit here (never defaulted inside the scripts).
37 7 1 * * cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/isa_briefing.py --amount 1000000 --mode codex-cli >> $LOG_DIR/isa_briefing.log 2>&1

# Outcome tracker — 06:00 KST daily
# US regular session closes at 05:00 KST. Running outcome tracker at 06:00
# catches each day's full close (both KR previous-day and US overnight) in
# one pass without colliding with the 00:00 US mid-session briefing.
0 6 * * * cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/outcome_tracker.py >> $LOG_DIR/outcome_tracker.log 2>&1

# Weekly calibration aggregator — Sunday 22:00 KST
# Pure Python; reads predictions.db, writes reports/weekly-calibration-YYYY-MM-DD.md
# and rolls state/calibration-trend.json (last 12 weeks).
0 22 * * 0 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/weekly_calibration.py >> $LOG_DIR/weekly_calibration.log 2>&1

# Weekly gold trend analysis — Sunday 21:00 KST (before the 22:00 calibration).
# Deterministic KRX-gold technical + macro scorecard + one LLM summary paragraph.
# Emits ACCUMULATE/HOLD/PAUSE to Telegram + reports/gold-trend-YYYY-MM-DD.md and
# rolls state/gold_trend.json (12 weeks). Refresh data/gold_macro_factors.yaml quarterly.
0 21 * * 0 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/gold_trend.py --llm-mode codex-cli >> $LOG_DIR/gold_trend.log 2>&1

# Learned-blend capstone readiness monitor — Monday 08:13 KST
# Pure read; counts CLOSED predictions carrying pillar components and sends a
# one-shot Telegram ping (then writes state/capstone_ready.flag) once >=100
# qualify, so the data-blocked learned-blend capstone can be built. Override the
# threshold with CAPSTONE_MIN_CLOSED. No-op until the threshold is crossed.
13 8 * * 1 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/capstone_readiness.py >> $LOG_DIR/capstone_readiness.log 2>&1

# Paper-trading tick — TWICE daily. Simulated long-only books (US $100k / KR ₩100M)
# trade the day's logged LIVE BULL predictions and record NAV to data/paper_trading.db.
# EOD-ish, not intraday; each run processes a trailing 7-day window, idempotent per
# (account, date), so a missing/incomplete bar is carried safely. Run at 06:30 KST
# (after the US overnight close, post outcome-tracker) and 16:00 KST (after the KR
# 15:30 close) so each market's just-closed session is captured. Bootstrap history
# once with `--replay FROM..TO` (see docs/stage-19/paper-trading-system.md).
30 6 * * * cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/paper_trading_run.py --market ALL >> $LOG_DIR/paper_trading.log 2>&1
0 16 * * * cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/paper_trading_run.py --market ALL >> $LOG_DIR/paper_trading.log 2>&1

# Weekly paper-trading review — Sunday 22:30 KST (after the weekly calibration).
# Advisory P&L attribution + tuning recommendations →
# reports/paper-trading-review-YYYY-MM-DD.md. Apply changes via PR.
30 22 * * 0 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/paper_trading_review.py >> $LOG_DIR/paper_trading_review.log 2>&1

# Watchlist monitor — DELAYED / EOD-ish, NOT real-time.
# Evaluates triggers against the latest CLOSE (provider.get_current_price returns
# the last bar; KR PyKRX is EOD-oriented), so this is a near-close checkpoint, not
# an intraday tick alerter. The script self-gates on market hours, so the cron
# windows below are intentionally coarse and the monitor no-ops cleanly when a
# market is closed.
#   KR window: every 30 min, 09:00-15:30 KST Mon-Fri (catches the KR close read).
0,30 9-15 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/watchlist_monitor.py --market KR >> $LOG_DIR/watchlist_monitor.log 2>&1
#   US window: every 30 min across the US session in KST for BOTH DST regimes.
#   The DST-aware gate (America/New_York) keeps the script a no-op outside RTH,
#   so the cron just has to span 22:30-06:30 KST: EDT close ~05:00 KST, EST close
#   ~06:00 KST (+30 min EOD grace → up to 06:30 KST). Split into the evening leg
#   (22-23 KST, Mon-Fri) and the overnight/morning leg (00-06 KST, Tue-Sat) so
#   day-of-week filters match the US trading calendar.
0,30 22-23 * * 1-5 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/watchlist_monitor.py --market US >> $LOG_DIR/watchlist_monitor.log 2>&1
0,30 0-6 * * 2-6 cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/watchlist_monitor.py --market US >> $LOG_DIR/watchlist_monitor.log 2>&1

# === Monthly news keyword-bucket audit (stage 6, report-only) ===
# First Sunday-ish: 1st of each month 20:00 KST. Samples recent live headlines,
# has Codex judge the keyword buckets (precision/misses/suggested edits),
# writes reports/news-bucket-audit-YYYY-MM-DD.md. Human applies edits via PR.
0 20 1 * * cd $PROJECT && uv run python scheduler/news_bucket_audit.py >> $LOG_DIR/news_bucket_audit.log 2>&1
